  {
   "id": "phone",
   "title": "Finding phone numbers, one refinement at a time",
   "topic": "3. Quantifiers",
   "blurb": "From the literal 555 to a pattern with boundaries and groups.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "title": "Start with the literal text",
     "text": "The simplest pattern is the text itself. 555 finds every 555, including the ones inside Room 5550 and Part 1555-0199, which are not phone numbers.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "match",
      "pattern": "555",
      "flags": "",
      "lines": [
       {
        "text": "Call 555-0199 today",
        "spans": [
         [
          5,
          8,
          0
         ]
        ],
        "note": ""
       },
       {
        "text": "Fax: 555-0123 or 555-0177",
        "spans": [
         [
          5,
          8,
          0
         ],
         [
          17,
          20,
          0
         ]
        ],
        "note": ""
       },
       {
        "text": "Room 5550 is closed",
        "spans": [
         [
          5,
          8,
          0
         ]
        ],
        "note": ""
       },
       {
        "text": "Part 1555-0199 is back-ordered",
        "spans": [
         [
          6,
          9,
          0
         ]
        ],
        "note": ""
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "title": "Say what the shape is",
     "text": "A phone number is three digits, a hyphen, four digits. \\d is one digit and {3} means exactly three of them. The room number is no longer matched, but 555-0199 inside Part 1555-0199 still is.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "match",
      "pattern": "\\d{3}-\\d{4}",
      "flags": "",
      "lines": [
       {
        "text": "Call 555-0199 today",
        "spans": [
         [
          5,
          13,
          0
         ]
        ],
        "note": ""
       },
       {
        "text": "Fax: 555-0123 or 555-0177",
        "spans": [
         [
          5,
          13,
          0
         ],
         [
          17,
          25,
          0
         ]
        ],
        "note": ""
       },
       {
        "text": "Room 5550 is closed",
        "spans": [],
        "note": ""
       },
       {
        "text": "Part 1555-0199 is back-ordered",
        "spans": [
         [
          6,
          14,
          0
         ]
        ],
        "note": ""
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "title": "Add word boundaries",
     "text": "\\b is a position between a word character and a non-word character. Putting it at both ends means the digits cannot be part of a longer run, so Part 1555-0199 is rejected.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "match",
      "pattern": "\\b\\d{3}-\\d{4}\\b",
      "flags": "",
      "lines": [
       {
        "text": "Call 555-0199 today",
        "spans": [
         [
          5,
          13,
          0
         ]
        ],
        "note": ""
       },
       {
        "text": "Fax: 555-0123 or 555-0177",
        "spans": [
         [
          5,
          13,
          0
         ],
         [
          17,
          25,
          0
         ]
        ],
        "note": ""
       },
       {
        "text": "Room 5550 is closed",
        "spans": [],
        "note": ""
       },
       {
        "text": "Part 1555-0199 is back-ordered",
        "spans": [],
        "note": ""
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "title": "Group the two halves",
     "text": "Parentheses capture parts of the match so the code can use them separately. Colours show whole match (orange), group 1 (green) and group 2 (blue).",
     "visual": {
      "type": "match",
      "pattern": "\\b(\\d{3})-(\\d{4})\\b",
      "flags": "",
      "lines": [
       {
        "text": "Call 555-0199 today",
        "spans": [
